{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "4f0c2b1e-7a0d-4a57-9d5e-6f2e8b1c3a90",
    "name": "Animal Picture API",
    "description": "Every request the animal-picture-api supports.\n\nStart the app first (`docker compose up --build` in the project folder). The API is then at http://localhost:3000, which is the `baseUrl` variable of this collection (see the **Variables** tab).\n\nEvery request has a small check in its **Tests** tab. Use **Run collection** to run them all in order: the \"Fetch and save\" requests come first, so the \"Latest picture\" and \"One picture by id\" requests always have a picture to find.\n\n**Good to know**\n- The requests in \"Fetch and save\" download real pictures from the internet and save them in your database.\n- Through the web page's address (http://localhost:8080) only `/api/...` requests are passed on to the API, so `/health` doesn't work there.\n- An animal that is switched off in `ENABLED_ANIMALS` answers 400. The checks here assume the default settings (cat, dog and bear switched on, at most 10 pictures per request).",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Health",
      "description": "Is the API running, and can it reach its database?",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Health check",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/health",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "health"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Answers `200 {\"status\":\"ok\",\"database\":\"up\"}` when everything works, or `503 {\"status\":\"degraded\",\"database\":\"down\"}` when the database can't be reached. Docker uses this to decide whether the API container is healthy."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('the API and its database are up', () => {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json()).to.eql({ status: 'ok', database: 'up' });",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Fetch and save",
      "description": "POST /api/pictures downloads new pictures from the picture services and saves them.\n\n- `animal` (optional): `cat`, `dog`, `bear` or `random`. Left out, the `DEFAULT_ANIMAL` setting is used. With `random`, each picture gets its own random animal.\n- `count` (optional): how many pictures, from 1 to `MAX_PICTURES_PER_REQUEST` (10 by default). Defaults to 1.\n\nA request saves all its pictures or none: if one download fails, the answer is `502` and nothing is saved.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "One picture, default animal",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/pictures",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "pictures"
              ]
            },
            "description": "No parameters: one picture of the animal set in `DEFAULT_ANIMAL`."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('answers 201 Created with 1 saved picture', () => {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(201);",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().count).to.eql(1);",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().pictures).to.have.lengthOf(1);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('every picture has its details and a url to the file', () => {",
                  "  for (const picture of pm.response.json().pictures) {",
                  "    pm.expect(picture).to.have.all.keys('id', 'animal', 'provider', 'sourceUrl', 'contentType', 'sizeBytes', 'createdAt', 'url');",
                  "    pm.expect(picture.contentType).to.match(/^image\\//);",
                  "    pm.expect(picture.url).to.eql(`/api/pictures/${picture.id}`);",
                  "  }",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "// Remember the newest picture, for \"One picture by id\".",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('pictureId', pm.response.json().pictures.at(-1).id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "One cat",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/pictures?animal=cat",
